(7660589, 1248135, 67145, '<td valign="top">it really is very disappointing that ppl vote on assumptions .. <br/>your title had no bearing on how much i liked this .. it was like a will-o-wisp passing thru my mind .. the impact for me was in the visual .. <br/>but i was blown away by all the low votes on some amazing images in this challenge .. of course ppl do have different tastes .. but like i say .. disappointing .. i personally never give a score less than 5 ... i feel if someone is going to go to the trouble of entering a photo i''ll give them points for that .. :)</td>', 'it really is very disappointing that ppl vote on assumptions .. your title had no bearing on how much i liked this .. it was like a will-o-wisp passing thru my mind .. the impact for me was in the visual .. but i was blown away by all the low votes on some amazing images in this challenge .. of course ppl do have different tastes .. but like i say .. disappointing .. i personally never give a score less than 5 ... i feel if someone is going to go to the trouble of entering a photo i''ll give them points for that .. :)', '2020-04-29 06:53:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7660590, 1247956, 67145, '<td valign="top">this is gorgeous .. soft and almost luxurious .. <br/>once again i see a wonderful abstract .. and notice the low votes .. <br/>so many wonderful and imaginative images in this challenge got really low votes .. <br/>so disappointing .. makes this site feel quite unwelcoming actually ... and yes i know ppl have different tastes .. but 2''s and 3''s i would think should be reserved for total crap .. excuse the french .. <br/></td>', 'this is gorgeous .. soft and almost luxurious .. once again i see a wonderful abstract .. and notice the low votes .. so many wonderful and imaginative images in this challenge got really low votes .. so disappointing .. makes this site feel quite unwelcoming actually ... and yes i know ppl have different tastes .. but 2''s and 3''s i would think should be reserved for total crap .. excuse the french .. ', '2020-04-29 07:02:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(7660591, 1248112, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by primabarbara:</b></div><hr/><i> This is fabulous, Roz. Congrats on TT<br/> <br/>Glad you didn''t crop it - the upper part is interesting and abstract enough! If if cropping at all then crop it at the bottom and on the sides and make a square out of it<br/>But how did you do it? Just shoot into your sink from above? And then? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thankyou so much for your comment Barbara .. i kept the bottom so there was more of the ''funnel'' coming down from the ''space ship'' .. into the darkness sort of .. like a bit foreboding .. <br/>i took many of photos of water coming out of the tap in my kitchen sink onto the vegetable steamer .. i''d take a heap of shots and then upload them onto the computer and check them out .. i did that several times ..i wanted the water totally in focus and a pleasing composition as well .. not an easy thing to get especially as the tap was getting in the way of the lens .. i tried 3 different lenses in my attempts as well .. i''ve never done anything like this before so it was a real learning curve  .. water does have a mind of its own .... anyway when i saw this one i felt i had the one i wanted .. i rotated the image in photoshop and then did a heap of stuff to it ...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2020-04-29 06:11:03.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by primabarbara: This is fabulous, Roz. Congrats on TT Glad you didn''t crop it - the upper part is interesting and abstract enough! If if cropping at all then crop it at the bottom and on the sides and make a square out of itBut how did you do it? Just shoot into your sink from above? And then?   thankyou so much for your comment Barbara .. i kept the bottom so there was more of the ''funnel'' coming down from the ''space ship'' .. into the darkness sort of .. like a bit foreboding .. i took many of photos of water coming out of the tap in my kitchen sink onto the vegetable steamer .. i''d take a heap of shots and then upload them onto the computer and check them out .. i did that several times ..i wanted the water totally in focus and a pleasing composition as well .. not an easy thing to get especially as the tap was getting in the way of the lens .. i tried 3 different lenses in my attempts as well .. i''ve never done anything like this before so it was a real learning curve  .. water does have a mind of its own .... anyway when i saw this one i felt i had the one i wanted .. i rotated the image in photoshop and then did a heap of stuff to it ...', '2020-04-29 07:09:14.000000', '2020-04-29 07:11:03.000000', 0),
(7660592, 1247605, 3306, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the Blue and personal best. The more I look at it the more I like it. To me it looks like Spermatozoa. Is that what you had in mind with your title? <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2020-04-29 06:34:30.</i></td>', 'Congrats on the Blue and personal best. The more I look at it the more I like it. To me it looks like Spermatozoa. Is that what you had in mind with your title? ', '2020-04-29 07:33:23.000000', '2020-04-29 07:34:30.000000', 0),
(7660593, 1248110, 3306, '<td valign="top">So nicely done. Such a modernistic feeling. I really like the subdued colors and lighting. Well deserved ribbon.</td>', 'So nicely done. Such a modernistic feeling. I really like the subdued colors and lighting. Well deserved ribbon.', '2020-04-29 07:37:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(7660594, 1248112, 98565, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/> <br/>i took many of photos of water coming out of the tap in my kitchen sink onto the <b>vegetable steamer</b> .. i''d take a heap of shots and then upload them onto the computer and check them out .. i did that several times ..i wanted the water totally in focus and a pleasing composition as well .. not an easy thing to get especially as the tap was getting in the way of the lens .. i tried 3 different lenses in my attempts as well .. i''ve never done anything like this before so it was a real learning curve  .. water does have a mind of its own .... anyway when i saw this one i felt i had the one i wanted .. i rotated the image in photoshop and then did a heap of stuff to it ... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for explaining me. Finally I unterstand that the vergetable steamer is a circular basket anyway - I didn''t get that before ... I use a pressure cooker so this item wasn''t familiar to me... lol</td>', 'Originally posted by roz:  i took many of photos of water coming out of the tap in my kitchen sink onto the vegetable steamer .. i''d take a heap of shots and then upload them onto the computer and check them out .. i did that several times ..i wanted the water totally in focus and a pleasing composition as well .. not an easy thing to get especially as the tap was getting in the way of the lens .. i tried 3 different lenses in my attempts as well .. i''ve never done anything like this before so it was a real learning curve  .. water does have a mind of its own .... anyway when i saw this one i felt i had the one i wanted .. i rotated the image in photoshop and then did a heap of stuff to it ...   Thanks for explaining me. Finally I unterstand that the vergetable steamer is a circular basket anyway - I didn''t get that before ... I use a pressure cooker so this item wasn''t familiar to me... lol', '2020-04-29 07:39:26.000000', NULL, 0),
